# SWARM behind Caddy (deploy/vps). The site address is SWARM's own public base URL —
# the same value the app reads as WEBHOOK_CALLBACK_BASE_URL — so the domain is set
# once, in .env. Caddy obtains and renews the certificate itself (ports 80 and 443
# must reach this host, and the domain's DNS record must point at it).
#
# One upstream, no path rules: the all-in-one control plane serves the webhook
# routes, /worker/* (including the WebSocket upgrade), /operator/*, /auth/*,
# /trpc/* and the dashboard. reverse_proxy passes Host and X-Forwarded-Proto
# through, which the session cookie's Secure flag and the webhook callback URL
# rely on.
{$WEBHOOK_CALLBACK_BASE_URL} {
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
